      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Severity: the ASPCA genus entry (Oxalis spp.) lists dogs and cats as toxic (tremors, drooling, kidney failure rare); NC State rates the plant low severity and says serious effects need large amounts, and that kidney failure is possible after serious ingestion. Graded 2 for pets (higher of the two, rule 5) and 1 for children; the 01e baseline was 1. Kidney failure is rare, listed as a symptom for completeness. The plant goes dormant (NC State, reduce watering until growth returns), but no source gives a rest factor in numbers. Light: NC State full sun to partial shade, RHS partial shade; stored bright indirect. Temperature and humidity: no usable figure (RHS rates it hardy outdoors, which is irrelevant indoors). RHS makes no toxicity statement."
      },
